      Some data analysts close this gap in a shorter, more focused stretch once SQL, Python, and
      statistics are already solid from real day-job practice. Others need a longer stretch, especially if
      coding is genuinely new. Let your own project readiness decide when you are ready to apply, not a
      fixed number of months you read somewhere else.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    For a step-by-step skill sequence once you are ready to specialise, the
    <a href="/blog/skill-roadmaps/machine-learning-roadmap-india/">machine learning roadmap for India</a>
    walks through the math prerequisites, the Python and ML toolkit build order, and the project-based
    sequence that gets interviews. If you want to see how this same decision plays out one step over, from
    machine learning engineering into data science and back, the
    <a href="/blog/ai-future/machine-learning-vs-data-science-career-path-india/">machine learning vs data
    science career path India</a> comparison covers that adjacent decision in depth.
  </p>

  <p>
    If you are earlier in this decision and still choosing between data analytics and a nearby role like
    business analysis, the
    <a href="/blog/skills/business-analyst-vs-data-analyst-career-india/">business analyst vs data analyst
    career India</a> guide covers that specific fork before you even get to the AI-engineering question.
  </p>

